    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Great Northern Railway built its line in 1903, a temporary camp called Harrisburg sprang up east of Fortine Creek, but the permanent station was placed on the west side, prompting businesses to relocate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        2
      ],
